The proposed solution correctly finds 22 and the six permutations of 123, but it wrongly excludes single-digit numbers. For a one-digit number n = d, the "product of the digits" is d and the "sum of the digits" is also d, so every digit 1–9 satisfies the condition (the claim that plural digits are required is an unjustified restriction). These contribute 1+2+...+9 = 45.

Total: 45 + 22 + 1332 = 1399.

